      "writtenOn": "2023-06-14T10:56:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If you want to implement this in more than one commit, it would probably have been easier to rework `read_swiotlb_info_from` to extract the non-verifying DT parsing into a constructor first (in pvmfw only) e.g.\n```\nfn read_swiotlb_info_from(fdt: \u0026Fdt) -\u003e libfdt::Result\u003cSwiotlbInfo\u003e {\n    let swiotlb \u003d Swiotlb::new_from_fdt(fdt)?;\n    if let Some(addr) \u003d swiotlb.addr {\n        if addr.checked_add(swiotlb.size).is_none() {\n        return Err(FdtError::BadValue);\n    }\n\n    Ok(swiotlb)\n}\n```\nbefore moving `SwiotlbInfo` to vmbase as a whole than removing the function and creating the constructor in `vmbase::...::SwiotlbInfo::new_from_fdt` then reintroducing the function and modifying the constructor, IMO.",
      "parentUuid": "26b0ff1c_58de4e35",
